{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210731,"nonce":"H7zJ+ooZ5siM3ZXcM3/0gaHS9R8=","title":"wlift_aot_sm_load_arg read frames.last() instead of frames[active_depth+1] on resume","message":"Fixed in commit 0611a6d. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n`wlift_aot_sm_load_arg(fiber, slot)` is called by every\n`CrossFnCallResume` block's lowering to recover the receiver + args\nthe matching Init stashed in the callee's slot table.\n\nThe implementation read `frames.last()` — correct on the initial\ninvoke (one frame just pushed, on top) but wrong on every resume\nafter a yield: the chain of pushed frames stays on the stack across\nsuspensions, so `frames.last()` now points at the deepest leaf\n(the innermost yielding callee), not at THIS parent's direct\ncallee.\n\n\n`Fiber.new { r.readAll }.try()` patterns. After the first WouldBlock\nyield bubbled up the closure → readAll → readRaw_ → withTryFn\nchain (frame stack depth 4), the second `fib.try()` re-entered the\noutermost closure body's resume entry. Its `load_arg(0)` read slot-0\nof the innermost-closure frame (an inner closure object) instead\nof slot-0 of the readAll callee frame (the Reader instance). The\nsubsequent dispatch resolved `Closure.readAll` →\nmethod-not-found → fiber marked Done with null, silently swallowing\nthe remaining work.\n\nDiagnostic signature in `WLIFT_AOT_TRACE_SM=1`:\n\n```\nSM-INIT-LOAD depth=0 frames_len=4 slot=0 v_id=v0 value=obj(Closure@…)\nSM-INVOKE depth=0 kind_in=0 Fn.readAll -\u003e method-not-found kind_out=2\n```\n\n`frames_len=4` shows the chain is still on the stack;\n`value=obj(Closure@…)` for what should have been the Reader\ninstance is the smoking gun.\n\n\nRead from `frames[active_depth + 1]`. The parent's frame is at\n`aot_active_depth`; its direct callee is therefore at +1.\nFall back to `frames.last()` only when the index is out-of-range\n(defensive).\n\n\n- `aot_runtime`: still 21/21\n- `events.spec`: 36/36\n- `proc.spec`: 30/33 → **32/33** (the 2 multi-iteration streaming\n  tests now pass; 1 SSE-style chunked test remains, separate bug)\n- `http.spec`: 24/25 (same single SSE chunked-streaming case)\n- `io.spec`: still hangs on `readLine` for BufferReader pattern\n  — separate bytes-to-list corruption bug\n\n\nThe remaining streaming failure isn't `load_arg` — it's a\nbuffer-bytes-to-list ordering issue. Symptom: `readLine` calls\n`readRaw_` repeatedly, then `IoCore.bytesToString` aborts with\n\"bytes must be numbers\". `_lineBuf` (a Wren List) gets populated\nwith non-integer entries somehow. Likely a Subscript / Buffer\nindexing miscompile under AOT. Same root for the hatch site\ncatalog hang (`Toml.parse(resp.body)` fails because body bytes\narrive corrupted).","files":null}]}